course: dictionary
lesson: 1226
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Bulldog is a dog, but it can also be a brave person, and it can be a metal clip. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «Bulldogs were bred by people to have short noses and flat faces.» The words bred, noses and faces tell you this is about an animal, so bulldog means a breed of dog here.
explain: A person can be called a bulldog too. This means they are very stubborn and brave and never let go of a task. The phrase «bulldog spirit» means never giving up, even when things get hard.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. Does "a breed of dog with flat faces" fit the sentence? Yes. Does "a brave person who never gives up" fit a sentence about the dog's face? No. The meaning that fits is the right one.
fact: A bulldog is a breed of strong dog with a short, flat face, a big head, short legs and loose, wrinkly skin.
fact: «Bulldogs were bred by people to have short noses and flat faces.» Very flat-faced dogs often struggle to breathe.
fact: A bulldog can also be a person who is very stubborn and brave and never lets go of a task.
fact: A bulldog clip is a strong metal clip for holding papers together.
fact: "The British bulldog" is a symbol of Britain's toughness, and "British Bulldog" is also a rough chasing game that some schools no longer allow.
exercise: «Bulldogs were bred by people to have short noses and flat faces.» In this sentence, what is a bulldog? | *A breed of dog | A sports team | A metal clip for papers | A person who never gives up
exercise: A teacher says, «Ali has real bulldog spirit.» What does bulldog spirit mean? | Being scared of dogs | Being very slow and lazy | *Being brave and never giving up
exercise: What is a bulldog clip? | A dog with loose, wrinkly skin | A rough chasing game at school | A team name for a football club | *A strong metal clip for holding papers together
test: A bulldog has short legs and loose, wrinkly skin. What kind of thing is a bulldog here? | *A breed of strong dog | A person who is stubborn | A rough chasing game | A paper clip
test: Why might a writer call someone a bulldog? | Because they are very tiny | *Because they are stubborn, brave and never let go | Because they hold papers together | Because they have a short, flat face
exam: Jayden says bulldog can only mean a dog. Is he right? | No, but a bulldog is always a sports team | *No, a bulldog can also be a brave person or a metal clip | Yes, and it is always a game | Yes, a bulldog is only ever an animal
